Z||000006||Neal||10-10-2001||11:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR><B> Oh shuddap!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>You can't even tell cuz the tach only goes to 6K   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> again<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Do I smell jealousy?<P>To answer the real question 1st shift at or near redline and all the following gears at 5500.  And for normal driving 2500-3000.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Klown||10-11-2001||04:47 AM||||I've heard tha redline shifting isn't always the best thing for acceleration on cars with a weak top end.  I seem to remember an article in compact car magazine where they got better acceleration out of a ford focus by shifting a couple of hundred rpm before the redline.  The focus also has good low end torque but a weak top end.||||reg||5
